list_add(&src_info->list, &hvpipe_src_list);
Reason:
`retain_and_null_ptr(src_info)` frees the memory pointed to by `src_info` and sets the pointer to NULL. The subsequent call to `list_add` uses the now-NULL `src_info`, causing a null pointer dereference when the kernel tries to access the list head or next/prev pointers.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
spin_lock_irqsave(&hvpipe_src_list_lock, flags);
if (hvpipe_find_source(srcID)) { ...; kfree(src_info); return -EALREADY; }
list_add(&src_info->list, &hvpipe_src_list);
spin_unlock_irqrestore(&hvpipe_src_list_lock, flags);
